// Doc Perrin, unlicensed medic and augment tinkerer, who mutters to a stuffed pigeon named Statistic.
npc: doc_perrin
name: Doc Perrin
start: back [flag:met_perrin]
start: first

node: first
  on_enter: {flag:met_perrin}
  doc_perrin (distracted): "Do not touch the pigeon. Statistic is thinking. ...Yes, you can talk to me. Perrin. Doc, if I must be. I put things in people's wrist bands that the city would rather I did not."
  > "What can you put in mine?" -> wares
  > "What is wrong with the pigeon?" -> pigeon
  > "I need the bench." -> bench
  > "Goodbye." -> goodbye

node: pigeon
  doc_perrin (fond): "Nothing. Nothing is wrong with Statistic. Statistic is a stuffed pigeon, and the city has no category for that either. It is the best colleague I have ever had."
  > [!flag:sq_09_started] "You seem sad about it." -> lost
  > [flag:sq_09_started, item:anecdote, !flag:sq_09_done] "I found Anecdote." {service:perrin_reunion} -> reunited
  > "What can you put in my band?" -> wares
  > "Goodbye." -> goodbye

node: lost
  on_enter: {flag:sq_09_started}
  doc_perrin (quiet): "Statistic had a partner. Anecdote. An Auditor took it off my shelf last spring: unregistered avian-shaped object. It is in the evidence cabinet in the Reintegration office, tagged and stacked. I would go myself, but Statistic would not like me out of its sight. Do not tell Statistic I said so."
  > "I will see what I can do." -> goodbye

node: reunited
  doc_perrin (moved): "There. Statistic, look. Anecdote. ...It says it was not worried. It is lying beautifully."
  > "Glad to help." -> goodbye

node: wares
  on_enter: {+clue:memory_anchor_exists(doc_perrin)}
  doc_perrin: "A Signal Lens, which shows you what the robots can see. Thirty credits, and I will pretend not to know where I got it. There is also a Memory Anchor, which keeps a certain pleasant district from smudging your notebook; that one I build myself, twenty-five credits, and it only does anything in that district."
  > [credits>=30, !owns:signal_lens] "Fit the Signal Lens. (30 credits)" {service:perrin_signal_lens} -> fitted
  > [credits>=25, !owns:memory_anchor] "Build the Memory Anchor. (25 credits)" {service:perrin_memory_anchor} -> anchored
  > [owns:signal_lens] "About the Lens again." -> lens
  > "Not now." -> goodbye

node: anchored
  doc_perrin (pleased): "Wear it in the Lull and the Lull will not be able to smudge a word. Take it off anywhere else, to spare the power. And sleep here afterwards regardless."
  > "Anything else?" -> wares

node: fitted
  doc_perrin (pleased): "Wear it from the band menu. Do not look at the sun."
  > "Anything else?" -> wares
  > "Thanks." -> goodbye

node: lens
  doc_perrin: "It shows the cones of anything that can see you, through walls. It also shows you things about your own band you may not enjoy. Try it on a mirror."
  > "Thanks." -> goodbye

node: back
  doc_perrin (distracted): "Yes? ...Oh, you. Statistic says hello."
  > "What can you put in my band?" -> wares
  > "I need the bench." -> bench
  > [flag:sq_09_started, item:anecdote, !flag:sq_09_done] "I found Anecdote." {service:perrin_reunion} -> reunited
  > [!flag:sq_09_started] "Is Statistic all right? It seems low." -> lost
  > [flag:sq_09_started, !item:anecdote, !flag:sq_09_done] "About Anecdote." -> lost2
  > "Goodbye." -> goodbye

node: lost2
  doc_perrin (quiet): "The evidence cabinet, Reintegration office. A hasp, nothing clever. Wire cutters would be quicker than patience."
  > "Right." -> goodbye

node: bench
  on_enter: {flag:perrin_knows_parts}
  doc_perrin (interested): "Ah. Pallas. A coupler and a memory shard make a drive. A Form 12-C and a permit stamp make a cargo tag. I do not ask what the tag is for. Bring me the parts."
  > [can:craft_repaired_drive] "Build the drive." {service:craft_repaired_drive} -> built
  > [can:craft_cargo_tag] "Press the tag." {service:craft_cargo_tag} -> built
  > [credits>=25, !item:memory_shard] "Do you have a memory shard? (25 credits)" {service:buy_memory_shard} -> built
  > "Not yet." -> goodbye

node: built
  doc_perrin (pleased): "There. Statistic approves. Statistic approves of very little."
  > "Thank you." -> goodbye

node: goodbye
  doc_perrin: "Mind the bands. And the pigeon."
  end
